IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `au-interpretation-time`
IMPORT `au-part1-application`
IMPORT `au-part4-repeal`
IMPORT `au-part5-interpretation`
IMPORT `au-part6-service`
IMPORT `au-part7-powers`
IMPORT `au-seat`

-- Worked cases for the seat layer: at least one for every question, with the facts a real
-- person in the seat would state, and a case outside the encoding (an asserted NOTHING) wherever
-- the text can fail to give an answer. Every expected value is written from the text and a
-- calendar (2026-01-31 and 2026-02-28 are Saturdays; 2026-02-02 and 2026-03-02 are Mondays),
-- never copied from a run.

GIVETH A LIST OF DATE
`no days listed` MEANS LIST

GIVETH A LIST OF DATE
`2 March 2026 listed` MEANS LIST (YearMonthDay 2026 3 2)

GIVETH A LIST OF DATE
`2 February 2026 listed` MEANS LIST (YearMonthDay 2026 2 2)

GIVETH A LIST OF DATE
`10 11 and 12 March 2026 sittings` MEANS LIST (YearMonthDay 2026 3 10), (YearMonthDay 2026 3 11), (YearMonthDay 2026 3 12)

GIVETH A LIST OF DATE
`sixteen daily sittings from 3 March 2026` MEANS LIST (YearMonthDay 2026 3 3), (YearMonthDay 2026 3 4), (YearMonthDay 2026 3 5), (YearMonthDay 2026 3 6), (YearMonthDay 2026 3 7), (YearMonthDay 2026 3 8), (YearMonthDay 2026 3 9), (YearMonthDay 2026 3 10), (YearMonthDay 2026 3 11), (YearMonthDay 2026 3 12), (YearMonthDay 2026 3 13), (YearMonthDay 2026 3 14), (YearMonthDay 2026 3 15), (YearMonthDay 2026 3 16), (YearMonthDay 2026 3 17), (YearMonthDay 2026 3 18)

§ `Whether this Act applies to the Act that binds me (s 2)`

#ASSERT `Does the Acts Interpretation Act 1901 apply to the Act that binds me` FALSE
-- The Act shows a contrary intention: s 2(2).
#ASSERT NOT (`Does the Acts Interpretation Act 1901 apply to the Act that binds me` TRUE)

§ `Business days, financial years and sitting days (ss 2B, 2M)`

-- Monday 2 March 2026: a business day; Saturday 28 February and Sunday 1 March are not.
#ASSERT `Is this day a business day` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 2) `no days listed`
#ASSERT NOT (`Is this day a business day` (YearMonthDay 2026 2 28) `no days listed`)
#ASSERT NOT (`Is this day a business day` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) `no days listed`)
-- A public holiday on the Monday.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is this day a business day` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 2) `2 March 2026 listed`)
-- The financial year is 12 months from 1 July: 10 March 2026 is in the year that ends 30 June 2026; 1 July 2026 starts the next.
#ASSERT `On which day does the financial year that includes my day end` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 10) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 6 30
#ASSERT `On which day does the financial year that includes my day end` (YearMonthDay 2026 6 30) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 6 30
#ASSERT `On which day does the financial year that includes my day end` (YearMonthDay 2026 7 1) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2027 6 30
-- Sitting days: the House began sitting on 10, 11 and 12 March. The 2nd sitting day after 4 March is 11 March; there is no 4th.
#ASSERT `Which day is the Nth sitting day of the House after my day` 2 (YearMonthDay 2026 3 4) `10 11 and 12 March 2026 sittings` EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 3 11)
#ASSERT `Which day is the Nth sitting day of the House after my day` 3 (YearMonthDay 2026 3 4) `10 11 and 12 March 2026 sittings` EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 3 12)
#ASSERT `Which day is the Nth sitting day of the House after my day` 4 (YearMonthDay 2026 3 4) `10 11 and 12 March 2026 sittings` EQUALS NOTHING

§ `When the Act or instrument that binds me comes into operation (ss 3, 3A)`

-- WORKED CASE: an Act passed (Royal Assent) on 10 March 2026 that says nothing about when it comes into force: the 28th day after, 7 April 2026 (s 3A(2)); at the start of that day (s 3).
#ASSERT `On which day does the Act or instrument that binds me come into operation` `Act` `nothing` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 10) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 10) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 4 7)
#ASSERT `At what moment does the Act or instrument that binds me come into operation` `Act` `nothing` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 10) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 10) EQUALS JUST (`the start of the day` (YearMonthDay 2026 4 7))
-- WORKED CASE: an Act that says it comes into force on a day to be fixed later; before the day is fixed the text gives no day.
#ASSERT `On which day does the Act or instrument that binds me come into operation` `Act` `a day to be fixed later, not yet fixed` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 10) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 10) EQUALS NOTHING
-- ... and once the day is fixed as 1 June 2026, it comes into operation at the start of that day (s 3).
#ASSERT `On which day does the Act or instrument that binds me come into operation` `Act` `a day that has since been fixed` (YearMonthDay 2026 6 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 10) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 6 1)
#ASSERT `At what moment does the Act or instrument that binds me come into operation` `Act` `a day that has since been fixed` (YearMonthDay 2026 6 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 10) EQUALS JUST (`the start of the day` (YearMonthDay 2026 6 1))
-- WORKED CASE: subordinate legislation made on 10 March 2026 that says nothing: the text gives no day (NOTHING), for a legislative instrument, a notifiable instrument or another instrument alike.
#ASSERT `On which day does the Act or instrument that binds me come into operation` `legislative instrument` `nothing` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 10) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 10) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `On which day does the Act or instrument that binds me come into operation` `notifiable instrument` `nothing` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 10) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 10) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `On which day does the Act or instrument that binds me come into operation` `other instrument made under a power` `nothing` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 10) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 10) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `At what moment does the Act or instrument that binds me come into operation` `legislative instrument` `nothing` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 10) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 10) EQUALS NOTHING
-- An Act to alter the Constitution: the day of Royal Assent, 10 March 2026 (s 3A(3)).
#ASSERT `On which day does the Act or instrument that binds me come into operation` `Act to alter the Constitution` `nothing` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 10) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 10) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 3 10)
-- An Act that names 1 May 2026: s 3A does not apply to it, so that day (s 3A(1), s 3).
#ASSERT `On which day does the Act or instrument that binds me come into operation` `Act` `a particular day` (YearMonthDay 2026 5 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 10) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 5 1)
-- An instrument that names its own day.
#ASSERT `On which day does the Act or instrument that binds me come into operation` `legislative instrument` `a particular day` (YearMonthDay 2026 5 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 10) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 5 1)

§ `What happens to what I already have or owe if an Act is repealed or amended (s 7)`

#ASSERT `What happens to what I already have or owe when the Act is repealed or amended` `a right, privilege, obligation or liability acquired, accrued or incurred under it` FALSE EQUALS `it is left as it was, as if the affected Act or part had not been repealed or amended`
#ASSERT `What happens to what I already have or owe when the Act is repealed or amended` `a penalty, forfeiture or punishment incurred in respect of an offence committed against it` FALSE EQUALS `it is left as it was, as if the affected Act or part had not been repealed or amended`
#ASSERT `What happens to what I already have or owe when the Act is repealed or amended` `something not in force or existing when the repeal or amendment takes effect` FALSE EQUALS `it is not revived`
-- A contrary intention in the repealing Act: the text gives no answer.
#ASSERT `What happens to what I already have or owe when the Act is repealed or amended` `a right, privilege, obligation or liability acquired, accrued or incurred under it` TRUE EQUALS `section 7(2) gives no answer because a contrary intention appears`
#ASSERT NOT (`Does repealing the Act that repealed my old Act bring my old Act back` FALSE)
#ASSERT `Does repealing the Act that repealed my old Act bring my old Act back` TRUE

§ `The form I must use and the reasons I must be given (ss 25C, 25D)`

#ASSERT `Does my form meet the requirement if it does not comply strictly with the prescribed form` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Does my form meet the requirement if it does not comply strictly with the prescribed form` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `Are the written reasons I was given complete` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Are the written reasons I was given complete` TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Are the written reasons I was given complete` TRUE FALSE TRUE)

§ `Documents served on me (ss 28A, 29)`

#ASSERT `Was the document served on me in a way the Acts Interpretation Act allows` `a natural person` `delivering it to the person personally` FALSE
#ASSERT `Was the document served on me in a way the Acts Interpretation Act allows` `a natural person` `sending it by pre-paid post to the address of the place of residence or business of the person last known to the person serving the document` FALSE
#ASSERT `Was the document served on me in a way the Acts Interpretation Act allows` `a body corporate` `leaving it at the head office, a registered office or a principal office of the body corporate` FALSE
-- Personal delivery is listed for a natural person only; for a body corporate it needs another law or a court order.
#ASSERT NOT (`Was the document served on me in a way the Acts Interpretation Act allows` `a body corporate` `delivering it to the person personally` FALSE)
#ASSERT `Was the document served on me in a way the Acts Interpretation Act allows` `a body corporate` `delivering it to the person personally` TRUE
-- Posted properly: taken to be served when a letter would ordinarily be delivered, 5 March 2026; unless the contrary is proved (9 March 2026).
#ASSERT `On which day am I taken to have been served by post` TRUE TRUE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 3 5) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 3 5) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 3 5)
#ASSERT `On which day am I taken to have been served by post` TRUE TRUE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 3 5) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 3 9) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 3 9)
-- Not prepaid: s 29 gives no day.
#ASSERT `On which day am I taken to have been served by post` TRUE FALSE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 3 5) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 3 5) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Acting in an office (ss 33(4), 33A)`

-- Acting in a vacant office from 1 July 2026: 12 months, that day included, end on 30 June 2027 (s 2G).
#ASSERT `Until which day may I keep acting in a vacant office` (YearMonthDay 2026 7 1) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2027 6 30)
#ASSERT `Until which day may I keep acting in a vacant office` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 15) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2027 3 14)
-- The office I was acting in became vacant on 15 March 2026: 12 months from the day of the vacancy (the day is not counted) end on 15 March 2027, unless the appointer directs otherwise or the vacancy is filled first.
#ASSERT `Until which day may I keep acting after the office I was acting in became vacant` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 15) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 3 15) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 3 15) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2027 3 15)
#ASSERT `Until which day may I keep acting after the office I was acting in became vacant` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 15) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 3 15) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 6 1) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 6 1)
#ASSERT `Until which day may I keep acting after the office I was acting in became vacant` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 15) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 5 1) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 6 1) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 5 1)
-- 12 months after the office was created or became vacant (15 March 2026): 16 March 2026 to 15 March 2027.
#ASSERT `On which day do the 12 months of an appointment to act under a power to appoint run out` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 15) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2027 3 15)

§ `A periodic report to a Minister (s 34C)`

-- The period reported on ended 31 August 2025. Six months after: from 1 September 2025 to 28 February 2026, a Saturday; so Monday 2 March 2026 (s 36(2)); Tuesday 3 March if the Monday is a holiday.
#ASSERT `By which day must I furnish my periodic report to the Minister` FALSE (YearMonthDay 2025 8 31) `no days listed` EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 3 2)
#ASSERT `By which day must I furnish my periodic report to the Minister` FALSE (YearMonthDay 2025 8 31) `2 March 2026 listed` EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 3 3)
-- The Act sets its own period: s 34C(2) gives no day.
#ASSERT `By which day must I furnish my periodic report to the Minister` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2025 8 31) `no days listed` EQUALS NOTHING
-- Applying for more time, with the specified period 1 to 31 March 2026: in time on the last day, out of time the day after; no opinion, no application.
#ASSERT `Can I still ask the Minister for more time to furnish my report` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 3 31) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 31) `no days listed`
#ASSERT NOT (`Can I still ask the Minister for more time to furnish my report` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 4 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 31) `no days listed`)
#ASSERT NOT (`Can I still ask the Minister for more time to furnish my report` FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 3 15) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 31) `no days listed`)
-- Explaining a late report: the period ended 31 March 2026 (a Tuesday); 14 days after is 14 April 2026.
#ASSERT `By which day must I explain in writing why my report was late` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 31) `no days listed` EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 4 14)
-- What I am owed: the 15th sitting day after the Minister received my report on 2 March 2026 is 17 March 2026 (sittings on each day from 3 to 18 March).
#ASSERT `By which day must the Minister lay my report before a House when no extension was granted` `an ordinary reporting person` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 2) `sixteen daily sittings from 3 March 2026` EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 3 17)
#ASSERT `By which day must the Minister lay my report before a House when an extension was granted` `an ordinary reporting person` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 2) `sixteen daily sittings from 3 March 2026` EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 3 17)
-- ASIO, the Australian Signals Directorate and the Office of National Intelligence: s 34C(3) does not apply, and s 34C(6)(c) is disregarded; ASIS is outside the section.
#ASSERT `By which day must the Minister lay my report before a House when no extension was granted` `the Australian Security Intelligence Organisation` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 2) `sixteen daily sittings from 3 March 2026` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `By which day must the Minister lay my report before a House when an extension was granted` `the Office of National Intelligence` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 2) `sixteen daily sittings from 3 March 2026` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `By which day must the Minister lay my report before a House when no extension was granted` `the Australian Secret Intelligence Service` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 2) `sixteen daily sittings from 3 March 2026` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `By which day must the Minister lay my report before a House when an extension was granted` `the Australian Secret Intelligence Service` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 2) `sixteen daily sittings from 3 March 2026` EQUALS NOTHING
-- The Minister granted the extension on 2 March 2026: the 3rd sitting day after is 5 March 2026; and the same for my explanation of a late report received on 2 March 2026.
#ASSERT `By which day must the Minister lay my explanation and the extension before a House` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 2) `sixteen daily sittings from 3 March 2026` EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 3 5)
#ASSERT `By which day must the Minister lay my explanation for a late report before a House` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 2) `sixteen daily sittings from 3 March 2026` EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 3 5)
-- Too few sittings listed: the text answers nothing on these inputs.
#ASSERT `By which day must the Minister lay my explanation and the extension before a House` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 2) `no days listed` EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Counting my time (ss 36, 37A)`

-- WORKED CASE: thirty days from 1 January 2026. "From" leaves out 1 January, so the period is 2 to 31 January 2026; 31 January is a Saturday, so the thing may be done on Monday 2 February 2026 (s 36(1) item 5; s 36(2)).
#ASSERT `On which day does my period of days, weeks, months or years end` (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1) `begins from a specified day` 30 Days TRUE `no days listed` EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 2 2)
-- ... and Tuesday 3 February if Monday 2 February is a holiday or the office is closed all day.
#ASSERT `On which day does my period of days, weeks, months or years end` (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1) `begins from a specified day` 30 Days TRUE `2 February 2026 listed` EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 2 3)
-- If no Act requires or allows the thing to be done, the rest-day rule does not move the day.
#ASSERT `On which day does my period of days, weeks, months or years end` (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1) `begins from a specified day` 30 Days FALSE `no days listed` EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 1 31)
-- WORKED CASE: one month from 31 January 2025. From 1 February 2025 the month ends immediately before 1 March 2025, 28 February 2025 (a Friday) (s 2G).
#ASSERT `On which day does my period of days, weeks, months or years end` (YearMonthDay 2025 1 31) `begins from a specified day` 1 Months TRUE `no days listed` EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2025 2 28)
-- WORKED CASES: three years from 16 July 2025, five years from 15 January 2025 and from 1 September 2025, two years from 28 February 2024, one year from 29 February 2024: the Act never says how long a year is, so the text gives no day.
#ASSERT `On which day does my period of days, weeks, months or years end` (YearMonthDay 2025 7 16) `begins from a specified day` 3 Years TRUE `no days listed` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `On which day does my period of days, weeks, months or years end` (YearMonthDay 2025 1 15) `begins from a specified day` 5 Years TRUE `no days listed` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `On which day does my period of days, weeks, months or years end` (YearMonthDay 2025 9 1) `begins from a specified day` 5 Years TRUE `no days listed` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `On which day does my period of days, weeks, months or years end` (YearMonthDay 2024 2 28) `begins from a specified day` 2 Years TRUE `no days listed` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `On which day does my period of days, weeks, months or years end` (YearMonthDay 2024 2 29) `begins from a specified day` 1 Years TRUE `no days listed` EQUALS NOTHING
-- The same for weeks.
#ASSERT `On which day does my period of days, weeks, months or years end` (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1) `begins from a specified day` 2 Weeks TRUE `no days listed` EQUALS NOTHING
-- A length that is not a whole number of at least 1.
#ASSERT `On which day does my period of days, weeks, months or years end` (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1) `begins from a specified day` 0 Days TRUE `no days listed` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `On which day does my period of days, weeks, months or years end` (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1) `begins from a specified day` 1.5 Months TRUE `no days listed` EQUALS NOTHING
-- A period worded by its END does not have a counted length.
#ASSERT `On which day does my period of days, weeks, months or years end` (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1) `ends before a specified day` 30 Days TRUE `no days listed` EQUALS NOTHING
-- "After" a day leaves it out too: the same answer as "from".
#ASSERT `On which day does my period of days, weeks, months or years end` (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1) `begins after a specified day` 30 Days TRUE `no days listed` EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 2 2)
-- "At, on or with" a day counts it: 30 days from 1 January, that day included, end on 30 January 2026 (a Friday).
#ASSERT `On which day does my period of days, weeks, months or years end` (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1) `begins at, on or with a specified day` 30 Days TRUE `no days listed` EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 1 30)

-- THE READING THE ACT DOES NOT STATE: a week as 7 days and a year as 12 months.
-- Three years from 16 July 2025: from 17 July 2025, 36 months end on 16 July 2028, a Sunday; Monday 17 July 2028 if the Act requires or allows the thing to be done.
#ASSERT `On which day would my period end if a week were 7 days and a year were 12 months` (YearMonthDay 2025 7 16) `begins from a specified day` 3 Years FALSE `no days listed` EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2028 7 16)
#ASSERT `On which day would my period end if a week were 7 days and a year were 12 months` (YearMonthDay 2025 7 16) `begins from a specified day` 3 Years TRUE `no days listed` EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2028 7 17)
-- Five years from 15 January 2025: 15 January 2030, a Tuesday. Five years from 1 September 2025: 1 September 2030, a Sunday, so Monday 2 September 2030.
#ASSERT `On which day would my period end if a week were 7 days and a year were 12 months` (YearMonthDay 2025 1 15) `begins from a specified day` 5 Years TRUE `no days listed` EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2030 1 15)
#ASSERT `On which day would my period end if a week were 7 days and a year were 12 months` (YearMonthDay 2025 9 1) `begins from a specified day` 5 Years FALSE `no days listed` EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2030 9 1)
#ASSERT `On which day would my period end if a week were 7 days and a year were 12 months` (YearMonthDay 2025 9 1) `begins from a specified day` 5 Years TRUE `no days listed` EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2030 9 2)
-- Two years from 28 February 2024: 28 February 2026, a Saturday; Monday 2 March 2026.
#ASSERT `On which day would my period end if a week were 7 days and a year were 12 months` (YearMonthDay 2024 2 28) `begins from a specified day` 2 Years FALSE `no days listed` EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 2 28)
#ASSERT `On which day would my period end if a week were 7 days and a year were 12 months` (YearMonthDay 2024 2 28) `begins from a specified day` 2 Years TRUE `no days listed` EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 3 2)
-- One year from 29 February 2024: from 1 March 2024, 12 months end on 28 February 2025, a Friday.
#ASSERT `On which day would my period end if a week were 7 days and a year were 12 months` (YearMonthDay 2024 2 29) `begins from a specified day` 1 Years TRUE `no days listed` EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2025 2 28)
-- Two weeks from 1 January 2026: from 2 January, 14 days end on 15 January 2026 (a Thursday).
#ASSERT `On which day would my period end if a week were 7 days and a year were 12 months` (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1) `begins from a specified day` 2 Weeks TRUE `no days listed` EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 1 15)

-- Periods worded by their end.
#ASSERT `On which day does my period end when the Act ends it at with or before a named day` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 10) `ends before a specified day` TRUE `no days listed` EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 3 9)
#ASSERT `On which day does my period end when the Act ends it at with or before a named day` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 10) `ends at, on or with a specified day` TRUE `no days listed` EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 3 10)
-- Ending on Saturday 28 February 2026: Monday 2 March 2026.
#ASSERT `On which day does my period end when the Act ends it at with or before a named day` (YearMonthDay 2026 2 28) `ends at, on or with a specified day` TRUE `no days listed` EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 3 2)
-- Ending Saturday 28 February 2026, Monday 2 March listed: Tuesday 3 March 2026 (a Sunday and a holiday in a row are skipped).
#ASSERT `On which day does my period end when the Act ends it at with or before a named day` (YearMonthDay 2026 2 28) `ends at, on or with a specified day` TRUE `2 March 2026 listed` EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 3 3)
-- A period worded by its start has no end named by a day.
#ASSERT `On which day does my period end when the Act ends it at with or before a named day` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 10) `begins from a specified day` TRUE `no days listed` EQUALS NOTHING

-- Which of my days count.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does the day I am counting from count as part of my period` `begins from a specified day`)
#ASSERT NOT (`Does the day I am counting from count as part of my period` `begins after a specified day`)
#ASSERT NOT (`Does the day I am counting from count as part of my period` `ends before a specified day`)
#ASSERT `Does the day I am counting from count as part of my period` `between two days`
#ASSERT `Does the day I am counting from count as part of my period` `begins at, on or with a specified day`
#ASSERT `Does the day I am counting from count as part of my period` `continues until a specified day`
#ASSERT `Does the day I am counting from count as part of my period` `ends at, on or with a specified day`
#ASSERT `On which day does my period begin` (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1) `begins from a specified day` EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 1 2)
#ASSERT `On which day does my period begin` (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1) `begins after a specified day` EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 1 2)
#ASSERT `On which day does my period begin` (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1) `begins at, on or with a specified day` EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1)
#ASSERT `On which day does my period begin` (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1) `between two days` EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1)
-- A period worded by its end has no start named by a day.
#ASSERT `On which day does my period begin` (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1) `ends before a specified day` EQUALS NOTHING

-- Saturday, Sunday or holiday.
#ASSERT `Is the last day of my period a day I cannot act on because it is a Saturday a Sunday or a holiday` (YearMonthDay 2026 1 31) `no days listed`
#ASSERT `Is the last day of my period a day I cannot act on because it is a Saturday a Sunday or a holiday` (YearMonthDay 2026 2 1) `no days listed`
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the last day of my period a day I cannot act on because it is a Saturday a Sunday or a holiday` (YearMonthDay 2026 2 2) `no days listed`)
#ASSERT `Is the last day of my period a day I cannot act on because it is a Saturday a Sunday or a holiday` (YearMonthDay 2026 2 2) `2 February 2026 listed`
-- The last day on which I may act.
#ASSERT `What is the last day on which I may act if my period ends on a Saturday a Sunday or a holiday` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 1 31) `no days listed` EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 2 2
#ASSERT `What is the last day on which I may act if my period ends on a Saturday a Sunday or a holiday` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 1 31) `2 February 2026 listed` EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 2 3
#ASSERT `What is the last day on which I may act if my period ends on a Saturday a Sunday or a holiday` FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 1 31) `no days listed` EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 1 31
#ASSERT `What is the last day on which I may act if my period ends on a Saturday a Sunday or a holiday` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 1 30) `no days listed` EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 1 30
-- Am I in time? The period is 2 to 31 January 2026; 31 January is a Saturday.
#ASSERT `Am I in time if I act on this day` (YearMonthDay 2026 1 30) (YearMonthDay 2026 1 2) (YearMonthDay 2026 1 31) `no days listed`
#ASSERT `Am I in time if I act on this day` (YearMonthDay 2026 1 31) (YearMonthDay 2026 1 2) (YearMonthDay 2026 1 31) `no days listed`
#ASSERT `Am I in time if I act on this day` (YearMonthDay 2026 2 2) (YearMonthDay 2026 1 2) (YearMonthDay 2026 1 31) `no days listed`
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I in time if I act on this day` (YearMonthDay 2026 2 3) (YearMonthDay 2026 1 2) (YearMonthDay 2026 1 31) `no days listed`)
-- 2 February is the listed holiday. Section 36(2) moves the LAST day on to 3 February; it does not make 2 February a day that falls outside the period, so acting on it is still within time (whether the office is open to receive it is not a question of the period).
#ASSERT `Am I in time if I act on this day` (YearMonthDay 2026 2 2) (YearMonthDay 2026 1 2) (YearMonthDay 2026 1 31) `2 February 2026 listed`
#ASSERT `Am I in time if I act on this day` (YearMonthDay 2026 2 3) (YearMonthDay 2026 1 2) (YearMonthDay 2026 1 31) `2 February 2026 listed`
-- Before the period begins.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I in time if I act on this day` (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 1 2) (YearMonthDay 2026 1 31) `no days listed`)

-- Attaining an age (s 37A): the start of the anniversary of the date of birth.
#ASSERT `At what moment do I attain a given age` (YearMonthDay 2000 3 10) 18 EQUALS JUST (`the start of the day` (YearMonthDay 2018 3 10))
-- Born on 29 February 2000: 2018 has no 29 February, and the Act does not say what the anniversary is.
#ASSERT `At what moment do I attain a given age` (YearMonthDay 2000 2 29) 18 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `At what moment do I attain a given age` (YearMonthDay 2000 2 29) 20 EQUALS JUST (`the start of the day` (YearMonthDay 2020 2 29))
